1
00:00:08,253 --> 00:00:10,387
A detector clicks. Up.

2
00:00:10,467 --> 00:00:12,552
Was the electron up all along?

3
00:00:13,382 --> 00:00:16,169
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

4
00:00:16,249 --> 00:00:20,440
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and contemplation.

5
00:00:21,245 --> 00:00:24,928
In Part 2, one bowl of
liquid was seen as water,

6
00:00:25,008 --> 00:00:27,347
pus, a home and nectar.

7
00:00:27,427 --> 00:00:31,369
And no neutral liquid was found
underneath. Beings still agree.

8
00:00:31,449 --> 00:00:34,167
Not because a hidden
floor holds them together,

9
00:00:34,247 --> 00:00:36,871
but because they meet
along shared channels,

10
00:00:36,951 --> 00:00:38,560
and correct one another.

11
00:00:39,369 --> 00:00:44,986
A careful listener may say: that is fine
for ghosts and fish. Physics is different.

12
00:00:45,116 --> 00:00:49,031
Physics measures the world
as it is, from no one's side.

13
00:00:49,111 --> 00:00:52,323
Surely there, at least,
the given is solid.

14
00:00:53,138 --> 00:00:55,699
So in this part, I turn to physics.

15
00:00:56,513 --> 00:01:00,767
I am not a physicist. I report
two views as fairly as I can.

16
00:01:00,847 --> 00:01:03,906
Carlo Rovelli's relational
quantum mechanics.

17
00:01:03,986 --> 00:01:06,695
And Karen Barad's agential realism.

18
00:01:07,509 --> 00:01:10,037
I use them as echoes, not proofs.

19
00:01:10,117 --> 00:01:12,592
Emptiness does not depend on physics.

20
00:01:12,672 --> 00:01:14,960
And physics does not need my approval.

21
00:01:15,782 --> 00:01:16,993
But it is striking.

22
00:01:17,073 --> 00:01:21,925
Two careful thinkers, starting from
the laboratory and not from meditation,

23
00:01:22,005 --> 00:01:24,864
arrive close to what Nāgārjuna saw.

24
00:01:25,698 --> 00:01:27,955
The pattern is the same as before.

25
00:01:28,035 --> 00:01:31,882
Two ways of seeing, side
by side, three times.

26
00:01:31,962 --> 00:01:33,639
Then: which holds?

27
00:01:34,517 --> 00:01:36,370
First, a measured value.

28
00:01:37,202 --> 00:01:39,908
Take one small particle, an electron.

29
00:01:39,988 --> 00:01:44,269
Measure one of its properties,
say its spin along one direction.

30
00:01:44,349 --> 00:01:46,502
The detector clicks. Up.

31
00:01:47,321 --> 00:01:50,108
Surely the electron was up all along.

32
00:01:50,188 --> 00:01:52,200
The measurement only revealed it.

33
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:56,453
The value sat there, finished,
from the electron's own side.

34
00:01:56,533 --> 00:02:00,628
And the detector read it off, the
way I read the time from a clock.

35
00:02:01,437 --> 00:02:05,736
Or, and it is a big or, look
at how the value is formed.

36
00:02:06,553 --> 00:02:09,679
Quantum mechanics has long
resisted that picture.

37
00:02:09,759 --> 00:02:14,136
Before the measurement, the theory does
not give the electron a definite value at

38
00:02:14,216 --> 00:02:16,205
all. Only chances.

39
00:02:17,021 --> 00:02:19,332
Rovelli draws a plain conclusion.

40
00:02:19,412 --> 00:02:23,490
A physical value is not a property
a thing carries on its own.

41
00:02:23,570 --> 00:02:28,399
It is a fact that holds relative to
another system, in an interaction.

42
00:02:29,217 --> 00:02:32,484
Up is a fact for the detector
that met the electron.

43
00:02:32,586 --> 00:02:35,686
For a system that has not
interacted with either of them,

44
00:02:35,766 --> 00:02:37,728
it is not yet a fact at all.

45
00:02:38,546 --> 00:02:42,148
So the value is not stored
in the electron, waiting.

46
00:02:42,228 --> 00:02:45,355
It forms in the meeting.
Rovelli says it plainly.

47
00:02:45,435 --> 00:02:48,847
The world is not made of things
with their own properties.

48
00:02:48,927 --> 00:02:51,175
It is made of events of interaction.

49
00:02:51,977 --> 00:02:54,736
That is the same move
as the apple in Part 1.

50
00:02:54,816 --> 00:02:57,005
The red was not stored in the fruit.

51
00:02:57,085 --> 00:03:00,008
It arose with light, eye and attention.

52
00:03:00,088 --> 00:03:03,704
Here, even the most exact
measurement is a meeting.

53
00:03:03,784 --> 00:03:06,697
And what is measured is
what forms in that meeting.

54
00:03:07,509 --> 00:03:11,654
And even seen this way, nothing
is missing. The click is real.

55
00:03:11,734 --> 00:03:15,839
The record stays. And the
experiment can be repeated tomorrow,

56
00:03:15,919 --> 00:03:17,311
with the same result.

57
00:03:18,134 --> 00:03:21,021
Second, two observers compare notes.

58
00:03:21,821 --> 00:03:24,146
I measure the electron, and get up.

59
00:03:24,226 --> 00:03:26,483
Later you check, and you get up too.

60
00:03:26,563 --> 00:03:28,783
We compare notes, and they match.

61
00:03:29,601 --> 00:03:34,412
Surely that settles it. If the value
were only relative, why would we agree?

62
00:03:34,492 --> 00:03:37,347
We agree because the
electron really was up,

63
00:03:37,427 --> 00:03:40,499
from its own side, before
either of us looked.

64
00:03:40,579 --> 00:03:42,487
Agreement proves the given.

65
00:03:43,285 --> 00:03:48,046
Or, and again it is a big or, look
at how the agreement is formed.

66
00:03:48,857 --> 00:03:51,671
Critics put exactly this
question to Rovelli.

67
00:03:51,751 --> 00:03:55,502
His answer, worked out with
the philosopher Emily Adlam,

68
00:03:55,582 --> 00:03:58,482
is a rule they call
cross-perspective links.

69
00:03:59,301 --> 00:04:04,452
If I have measured the electron, and you
then interact both with the electron and

70
00:04:04,532 --> 00:04:08,433
with me, with my record,
my notes, my words,

71
00:04:08,513 --> 00:04:10,652
then your result will match my record.

72
00:04:11,449 --> 00:04:14,072
Agreement is real, and reliable.

73
00:04:14,152 --> 00:04:16,821
But it is formed through
the meeting between you,

74
00:04:16,924 --> 00:04:18,624
me and the electron.

75
00:04:18,704 --> 00:04:22,827
It does not need a hidden value
that existed before anyone met it.

76
00:04:23,658 --> 00:04:26,771
This is Candrakīrti's answer from Part 2,

77
00:04:26,851 --> 00:04:28,904
met again in a laboratory.

78
00:04:28,984 --> 00:04:32,478
There, healthy human eyes
agreed that the conch is white,

79
00:04:32,558 --> 00:04:37,754
and corrected the jaundiced eye, with
no judge standing outside every view.

80
00:04:38,593 --> 00:04:41,530
Here, observers agree by interacting.

81
00:04:41,610 --> 00:04:43,962
And errors are caught by checking again.

82
00:04:44,042 --> 00:04:48,187
Shared reality is built by
coordination and cross-checking.

83
00:04:48,267 --> 00:04:50,040
Not by standing on a floor.

84
00:04:50,845 --> 00:04:55,357
And even seen this way, nothing is
missing. Scientists still agree.

85
00:04:55,437 --> 00:04:59,438
Papers are still checked. Bridges
are still built from the numbers.

86
00:05:00,311 --> 00:05:02,572
Third, a stick in a dark room.

87
00:05:03,394 --> 00:05:07,608
Barad starts from Niels Bohr, one of
the founders of quantum mechanics,

88
00:05:07,688 --> 00:05:09,324
and an image Bohr liked.

89
00:05:10,142 --> 00:05:12,997
Picture walking through
a dark room with a stick.

90
00:05:13,077 --> 00:05:17,888
If I grip it firmly, the stick becomes
part of me. I do not feel the stick.

91
00:05:17,968 --> 00:05:19,768
I feel the wall at its tip.

92
00:05:20,573 --> 00:05:25,071
If I hold it loosely, the stick
becomes something I feel. Its weight.

93
00:05:25,151 --> 00:05:26,883
Its roughness in my hand.

94
00:05:27,705 --> 00:05:31,837
Surely there is a fixed line
between me, the one who observes,

95
00:05:31,917 --> 00:05:36,755
and the stick and the wall, the things
observed. The line is simply there.

96
00:05:36,835 --> 00:05:38,091
I only find it.

97
00:05:38,893 --> 00:05:43,206
Or, and it is the biggest or,
look at how the line is formed.

98
00:05:44,022 --> 00:05:48,752
With the same stick and the same hand,
the line falls in a different place,

99
00:05:48,832 --> 00:05:50,564
depending on how I hold it.

100
00:05:51,394 --> 00:05:53,774
Barad calls this the agential cut.

101
00:05:53,854 --> 00:05:59,045
A measuring setup, she says, does not
slice up a world already divided into

102
00:05:59,125 --> 00:06:02,351
observer and observed. It enacts the cut.

103
00:06:03,169 --> 00:06:07,110
It settles, for this meeting,
what counts as the instrument,

104
00:06:07,190 --> 00:06:09,176
and what counts as the object.

105
00:06:09,256 --> 00:06:11,961
And what a word like
position can even mean here.

106
00:06:12,041 --> 00:06:14,588
Change the setup, and the cut moves.

107
00:06:15,426 --> 00:06:19,776
Bohr showed that an experiment set up to
find which path a particle takes cannot

108
00:06:19,856 --> 00:06:23,390
also show the interference
that needs both paths.

109
00:06:23,470 --> 00:06:26,841
These are not two windows
onto one finished particle.

110
00:06:26,921 --> 00:06:30,527
They are two different
phenomena, each with its own cut.

111
00:06:31,329 --> 00:06:35,800
So Barad says that things do not
exist first, and then interact.

112
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:38,654
They emerge through what
she calls intra-action.

113
00:06:38,734 --> 00:06:43,060
Action within one phenomenon,
not between things already there.

114
00:06:43,861 --> 00:06:47,802
That is close to the bat, the
bee and the ant in Part 1.

115
00:06:47,882 --> 00:06:50,493
A different body singles
out a different world.

116
00:06:50,573 --> 00:06:54,949
The mountain, the one who meets it, and
the channel of meeting are designated

117
00:06:55,029 --> 00:06:59,967
together. Barad's cut is that
togetherness, seen in the laboratory.

118
00:07:00,785 --> 00:07:03,639
And even seen this way,
nothing is missing.

119
00:07:03,719 --> 00:07:06,072
I still find my way across the dark room.

120
00:07:06,152 --> 00:07:08,277
And I still do not walk into the wall.

121
00:07:09,093 --> 00:07:10,960
Now, where I part from them.

122
00:07:11,788 --> 00:07:16,644
Here I must be careful. Because this is
where the echo can turn into a new floor.

123
00:07:17,453 --> 00:07:20,271
It is easy to read both views this way.

124
00:07:20,374 --> 00:07:22,998
Things are not real, but relations are.

125
00:07:23,078 --> 00:07:26,127
Interactions are the
true stuff of the world.

126
00:07:26,230 --> 00:07:28,980
Phenomena are the real building blocks.

127
00:07:29,793 --> 00:07:34,699
Whatever the authors themselves intend,
that reading only moves the floor.

128
00:07:34,779 --> 00:07:37,484
Before, solid things sat underneath.

129
00:07:37,564 --> 00:07:39,717
Now, solid relations do.

130
00:07:40,525 --> 00:07:42,727
Nāgārjuna does not allow that.

131
00:07:42,807 --> 00:07:45,010
A relation needs what it relates.

132
00:07:45,090 --> 00:07:46,912
Between needs two sides.

133
00:07:46,992 --> 00:07:52,333
Take away the electron and the detector,
and no interaction is left standing on its

134
00:07:52,413 --> 00:07:53,613
own.

135
00:07:53,969 --> 00:07:58,934
Relations and the things related
arise together. Neither comes first.

136
00:07:59,733 --> 00:08:03,620
So the interaction is as
unfindable as the electron.

137
00:08:03,700 --> 00:08:07,755
And the cut is as unfindable
as the two sides it divides.

138
00:08:08,569 --> 00:08:12,606
What I meet is not a web of real
relations under the appearances.

139
00:08:12,686 --> 00:08:14,779
It is the appearances themselves.

140
00:08:14,859 --> 00:08:18,326
Vivid, working, and empty
all the way through.

141
00:08:18,406 --> 00:08:20,028
The relations included.

142
00:08:20,837 --> 00:08:24,371
Rovelli himself has written
about reading Nāgārjuna,

143
00:08:24,451 --> 00:08:28,936
and finding in him a way to think
about a world with no ultimate things.

144
00:08:29,016 --> 00:08:30,557
I am glad of the meeting.

145
00:08:31,390 --> 00:08:35,291
But I do not need physics to be
right for dependent arising to hold.

146
00:08:35,371 --> 00:08:39,734
And I do not need dependent arising
to settle what physics will say next.

147
00:08:39,814 --> 00:08:42,587
Scientific models are designations too.

148
00:08:42,667 --> 00:08:47,021
Among the most reliable ones I
have, inside their own fields.

149
00:08:47,834 --> 00:08:52,156
Two ways of seeing, three times
over, now in the laboratory.

150
00:08:52,236 --> 00:08:54,267
Which carries more valid truth?

151
00:08:55,073 --> 00:09:00,622
I test them as before. By experience.
By logic. And by how things work.

152
00:09:01,450 --> 00:09:05,976
By experience. What does any
physicist actually meet? A click.

153
00:09:06,056 --> 00:09:10,451
A trace on a screen. A number on
a display. A colleague's report.

154
00:09:11,257 --> 00:09:15,185
Never a value standing on
its own, before any meeting.

155
00:09:15,265 --> 00:09:18,378
That value is never met. It is supplied.

156
00:09:18,458 --> 00:09:22,961
By the same habit that supplies the
apple standing on its own in the bowl.

157
00:09:23,778 --> 00:09:27,978
By logic. If the electron's value
were fixed from its own side,

158
00:09:28,058 --> 00:09:31,918
it would be the same for
every system, met or not.

159
00:09:31,998 --> 00:09:35,496
And the cut would not move
with the setup. Both fail.

160
00:09:36,297 --> 00:09:39,940
And a relation put forward
as the new floor fails too.

161
00:09:40,020 --> 00:09:43,513
Picking it out needs the things
it relates. And they need it.

162
00:09:43,593 --> 00:09:45,664
Nothing in the chain stands alone.

163
00:09:46,490 --> 00:09:47,429
By working.

164
00:09:47,509 --> 00:09:52,008
The given view says physics works
because a finished world sits underneath,

165
00:09:52,088 --> 00:09:53,575
and measurement reads it.

166
00:09:54,390 --> 00:09:58,509
The formed view explains the
working fully. Measurements repeat.

167
00:09:58,589 --> 00:10:01,212
Observers agree. Predictions hold.

168
00:10:01,292 --> 00:10:04,079
Because these are patterns
meeting other patterns,

169
00:10:04,159 --> 00:10:06,597
reliably, along their channels.

170
00:10:07,413 --> 00:10:10,295
Working never needed a
floor. Not in the bowl.

171
00:10:10,375 --> 00:10:11,997
And not in the laboratory.

172
00:10:12,817 --> 00:10:16,500
So the given is not the
truer view, even in physics.

173
00:10:16,580 --> 00:10:21,070
It is the default view, carried
by habit, and by the way we talk.

174
00:10:21,906 --> 00:10:25,400
What fails is only the
extra claim: a value,

175
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:29,684
a thing, or a relation, standing
there from its own side.

176
00:10:30,489 --> 00:10:32,207
Nothing that works is lost.

177
00:10:33,074 --> 00:10:36,599
This is Part 3 of the
Dependent Arising series.

178
00:10:37,409 --> 00:10:40,114
In Part 4, I draw some conclusions.

179
00:10:40,194 --> 00:10:43,973
Without essence, does everything
turn ghostly and void?

180
00:10:44,053 --> 00:10:48,474
The car still knocks you down. It
still rains. And you still get sick.

